// `+` is trait-backed (`Add`). A plain struct is neither numeric nor `impl`s `Add`, so applying
// `+` to two of them is a static type error (`E0007`) — the operator-trait check now covers
// concrete user types, not only generics, catching what was previously a runtime failure.
// expect: error E0007 at 9:6
// expect: exit 1
struct P { x: int }
a = P { x: 1 };
b = P { x: 2 };
echo a + b;
